From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: check BO capacity before in-place linear conversion

Repeated full texture uploads can switch a 16x16 tiled resource to linear
without reallocating its BO. A 720-wide R8 texture needs a 768-byte linear
stride, which can exceed the original tiled allocation. In release builds,
the assertion does not prevent util_copy_rect from writing past the mapping.

Compute the prospective linear layout before changing the resource. Keep
the tiled layout and normal staging writeback when the existing BO is too
small. This preserves the optimization for layouts that fit.

Reproduced on Mali-G52 with a standalone GLES luminance upload/readback test
and Kodi's software-decoded 720x480 video. No decoder stride changes.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -2004,6 +2004,21 @@
    }
 }
 
+/* Linear rows can require more alignment than 16x16 tiles. The streaming
+ * optimization reuses the tiled BO, so only convert when the entire linear
+ * layout fits. Otherwise retain tiling and use the normal staging writeback.
+ */
+static bool
+panfrost_can_linear_convert_in_place(struct pipe_screen *screen,
+                                    struct panfrost_resource *prsrc)
+{
+   struct panfrost_resource linear = {.base = prsrc->base};
+
+   return panfrost_resource_try_setup(screen, &linear, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
+                                     prsrc->image.props.format, 0) &&
+          linear.plane.layout.data_size_B <= panfrost_bo_size(prsrc->bo);
+}
+
 /* Queue a CS modifier conversion job to calculate and store the payload sizes
  * of the current AFBC BO into a new AFBC-P payload layout BO. Returns true on
  * success. */
@@ -2389,13 +2404,14 @@
 
          if (prsrc->modifier ==
              DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ARM_16X16_BLOCK_U_INTERLEAVED) {
-            if (panfrost_should_linear_convert(ctx, prsrc, transfer)) {
+            if (panfrost_should_linear_convert(ctx, prsrc, transfer) &&
+                panfrost_can_linear_convert_in_place(screen, prsrc)) {
                pan_resource_afbcp_stop(prsrc);
                panfrost_resource_setup(screen, prsrc, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
                                        prsrc->image.props.format, 0);
 
-               /* converting the resource from tiled to linear and back
-                * shouldn't increase memory usage...
+               /* The prospective linear layout was checked before changing
+                * the resource's modifier or writing to the existing BO.
                 */
                assert(prsrc->plane.layout.data_size_B <= panfrost_bo_size(bo));
 
